# Journey — Agent Documentation Protocol

**Before any work:** Read `docs/PROJECT_STATUS.md`.

**Three living documents** (same pattern as Anima) — update after meaningful work:

1. **`AGENTS.md`** — protocol, machine notes, scripts, conventions (when those change)
2. **`PROJECT_REFERENCE_JOURNEY.md`** — full encyclopedia (when mechanics, architecture, data, AI, or screens change; bump Last updated / build / test count)
3. **`README.md`** — when you add, remove, or materially change **user-visible** features (writing tools, AI actions, settings, export/backup, shortcuts, platforms, install/releases)

Also update:

- `docs/PROJECT_STATUS.md` (status, changelog, next steps) — every session
- `docs/ROADMAP.md` when completing phase items

`docs/PROJECT_REFERENCE.md` is a **stub** that points at `PROJECT_REFERENCE_JOURNEY.md` — do not maintain a second copy.

**Versioning:** Keep `pubspec.yaml` at `1.0.0+<build>` — only increment the build number after `+`, never the `1.0.0` unless the user asks.

**Machine notes & scripts:** see `AGENTS.md` → *Machine notes* for this PC's toolchain (and the
"never build from an exFAT drive" rule), and *Automation scripts* for `scripts/setup_linux_dev.sh`
(fresh PC), `scripts/update_linux.sh` (desktop app), `./deploy.sh` (one-command release) and
`scripts/dev_copy_linux.sh`.

See `AGENTS.md` at repo root for full instructions.
